🔧 Predictive Maintenance & Simulation System

A Machine Learning powered system that predicts industrial equipment failure using real-time sensor data.
The project uses a Random Forest classification model and exposes predictions through a FastAPI REST API, allowing users to simulate machine conditions and analyze failure probability.

This project demonstrates predictive analytics, backend API development, and simulation modeling for real-world maintenance systems.

📌 Project Overview

Unexpected equipment failures can lead to high operational costs and downtime in industrial environments.
This system predicts potential failures based on sensor readings such as:

Temperature

Vibration

Pressure

Humidity

By analyzing these inputs, the model estimates the probability of machine failure, helping organizations take preventive maintenance actions before breakdowns occur.

🚀 Features

✅ Machine Failure Prediction using Machine Learning
✅ Random Forest classification model
✅ FastAPI-based REST API for real-time predictions
✅ Simulation engine to analyze failure under varying conditions
✅ JSON-based API responses
✅ Interactive API documentation with Swagger UI

🧠 Tech Stack

Python

Scikit-learn

FastAPI

NumPy

Pandas

Uvicorn


⚙️ Installation

Clone the repository

git clone https://github.com/pragatis26/PREDICTIVE_MAINTENANCE_AND_SIMULATION_SYSTEM.git
cd predictive-maintenance-system

Install dependencies

pip install -r requirements.txt
▶️ Running the API

Start the FastAPI server

uvicorn api.main:app --reload

The API will run at:

http://127.0.0.1:8000
📖 API Documentation

FastAPI automatically generates interactive documentation.

Open in browser:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
🔮 Prediction Endpoint

POST /predict

Predicts whether equipment will fail based on sensor data.

Example request:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/predict?temperature=90&vibration=0.08&pressure=55&humidity=65

Example response:

{
  "failure_prediction": 1,
  "failure_probability": 0.87
}
🔬 Simulation Endpoint

GET /simulate

Simulates machine behavior under changing conditions to analyze failure risk.

Example request:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/simulate?temperature=70&vibration=0.08&pressure=55&humidity=65

Example response:

{
  "simulation_results": [
    {
      "temperature": 70,
      "failure_prediction": 1,
      "failure_probability": 0.57
    },
    {
      "temperature": 75,
      "failure_prediction": 1,
      "failure_probability": 0.63
    }
  ]
}
🧪 Simulation Script

The project also includes a Python script that simulates sensor conditions and predicts failure probabilities.

Run:

python simulation/simulate.py

Example output:

{'temperature': 70, 'failure_prediction': 1, 'failure_probability': 0.57}
{'temperature': 75, 'failure_prediction': 1, 'failure_probability': 0.63}
{'temperature': 80, 'failure_prediction': 1, 'failure_probability': 0.73}
📊 Machine Learning Model

The system uses a Random Forest Classifier trained on simulated industrial sensor data.

Model inputs:

Temperature

Vibration

Pressure

Humidity

Model output:

Failure prediction (0 = Normal, 1 = Failure)

Failure probability score

The trained model is stored as:

model/model.pkl
